      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.08,
          "end": 4.95,
          "en": "Okay, let's now solve this together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.95,
          "end": 7.49,
          "en": "We wanna add a couple of API routes here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.49,
          "end": 10.8,
          "en": "so that we can have our own server-side logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.8,
          "end": 14.02,
          "en": "which is detached from rendering pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.02,
          "end": 15.89,
          "en": "And you'll learn how that works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.89,
          "end": 17.3,
          "en": "In the pages folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.3,
          "end": 22.3,
          "en": "you add that special API folder, which has to be called API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.88,
          "end": 25.07,
          "en": "And in there you can now again create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.07,
          "end": 28.04,
          "en": "any file and folder structure of your choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.04,
          "end": 31.57,
          "en": "to define the different API routes and the paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.57,
          "end": 34.84,
          "en": "leading to those routes you wanna use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.84,
          "end": 38.06,
          "en": "For example, we could add a newsletter JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.06,
          "end": 40.363,
          "en": "for the newsletter related logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.32,
          "end": 45.22,
          "en": "Then you learn that an API route in the end just is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.22,
          "end": 49.49,
          "en": "a function inside of that API route file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.49,
          "end": 52.63,
          "en": "which you should export like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.63,
          "end": 56.66,
          "en": "And this function receives a request and the response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.66,
          "end": 59.72,
          "en": "automatically passed in by next JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.72,
          "end": 63.93,
          "en": "when it executes this function for incoming requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.93,
          "end": 67.33,
          "en": "Here we can then check the request method, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.33,
          "end": 70.86,
          "en": "to only proceed for a post requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.86,
          "end": 74.67,
          "en": "And we can do this here for the email registration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.67,
          "end": 77.73,
          "en": "because whilst this is the only kind of method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.73,
          "end": 79.14,
          "en": "I wanna support here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.14,
          "end": 82.38,
          "en": "I wanna make sure that no other method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.38,
          "end": 84.53999999999999,
          "en": "triggers any logic here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.53999999999999,
          "end": 87.26,
          "en": "So I explicitly check if the incoming request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.26,
          "end": 91.31,
          "en": "is a post request and I only wanna proceed in that case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.31,
          "end": 94.87,
          "en": "because in that case I for example also know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.87,
          "end": 98.62,
          "en": "that I can extract data from the request body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.62,
          "end": 102.88300000000001,
          "en": "Because for example, get requests would not carry any data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.9,
          "end": 107.57,
          "en": "So with that, we can extract data from the request body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.57,
          "end": 109.96000000000001,
          "en": "and we can do it as with the request body field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.96000000000001,
          "end": 111.36,
          "en": "as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.36,
          "end": 114.97,
          "en": "Here, we could then expect that we have an email field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.97,
          "end": 116.61,
          "en": "and that's up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.61,
          "end": 119.50999999999999,
          "en": "You are the developer of this site.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.50999999999999,
          "end": 123.19,
          "en": "So it's up to you, how you transmit your data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.19,
          "end": 126.07,
          "en": "And I will therefore expect an email field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.07,
          "end": 128.67,
          "en": "So the user email is then extracted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.67,
          "end": 130.253,
          "en": "from the incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.31,
          "end": 133.85,
          "en": "Now here we could then also validate this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.85,
          "end": 137.21,
          "en": "and check if it's maybe not valid or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.21,
          "end": 138.883,
          "en": "if email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.77,
          "end": 141.13,
          "en": "user email I mean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.13,
          "end": 144.93,
          "en": "does maybe not include @ symbol.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.93,
          "end": 147.56,
          "en": "Which is a very basic email validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.56,
          "end": 150.63,
          "en": "you might want to implement more (indistinct) one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.63,
          "end": 152.07,
          "en": "but it's a start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.07,
          "end": 155.23,
          "en": "And such server-side validation is optional",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.23,
          "end": 157.35,
          "en": "but strongly recommended.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.35,
          "end": 161.4,
          "en": "Because even if you add validation and checks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.4,
          "end": 165.12,
          "en": "in your front-end code, those validation steps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.12,
          "end": 167.7,
          "en": "can always be circumvented.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.7,
          "end": 172.01,
          "en": "After all all your front-end code is exposed to your users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.01,
          "end": 174.34,
          "en": "so they could also manipulate it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.34,
          "end": 177.7,
          "en": "So you shouldn't rely on front-end validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.7,
          "end": 181.71,
          "en": "front-end validation is always just a convenience feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 181.71,
          "end": 183.54,
          "en": "for your users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.54,
          "end": 187.93,
          "en": "Instead to really make sure that you get valid data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.93,
          "end": 190.56,
          "en": "and that you work with valid data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 190.56,
          "end": 193.58,
          "en": "you should validate in your API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 193.58,
          "end": 198.57999999999998,
          "en": "because this code can't be viewed or changed by your users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.87,
          "end": 201.79,
          "en": "Now for this task here, it's optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201.79,
          "end": 204.77,
          "en": "I did not tell you to add such validation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 204.77,
          "end": 208.12,
          "en": "So if you did not do that, that's totally fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.12,
          "end": 210.14,
          "en": "I just wants to bring it up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.14,
          "end": 213.21,
          "en": "because it is important is to be aware of the role",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.21,
          "end": 216.2,
          "en": "server-side validation plays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 216.2,
          "end": 219.46,
          "en": "Now, here we could then return to cancel",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.46,
          "end": 222.61,
          "en": "the (indistinct) function execution if we make it in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 222.61,
          "end": 226.73,
          "en": "So if we have invalid data and we could return a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 226.73,
          "end": 229.2,
          "en": "with a status code of 422",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 229.2,
          "end": 231.7,
          "en": "which is a status code signaling that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 231.7,
          "end": 236.7,
          "en": "the user input was bad, and then maybe set a message of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 236.75,
          "end": 239.07999999999998,
          "en": "invalid email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 239.07999999999998,
          "end": 240.63,
          "en": "Something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.63,
          "end": 244.25,
          "en": "And we would send this response back to the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 244.25,
          "end": 246.43,
          "en": "if the input is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 246.43,
          "end": 249.9,
          "en": "And there after I return to cancel the function execution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 249.9,
          "end": 253.06,
          "en": "because I will add more code after this if check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 253.06,
          "end": 255.87,
          "en": "and I don't want to execute that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 255.87,
          "end": 260.09,
          "en": "if we have invalid input, hence the return statement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 260.09,
          "end": 263.33,
          "en": "Now, if we do make it past this if block though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 263.33,
          "end": 266.27,
          "en": "we know that we do have a valid user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 266.27,
          "end": 268.24,
          "en": "and then we could store it in a database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 268.24,
          "end": 270.12,
          "en": "or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 270.12,
          "end": 271.82,
          "en": "And for the moment we'll not do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 271.82,
          "end": 275.82,
          "en": "for the moment I'll just console log, that user email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 275.82,
          "end": 278.92,
          "en": "And that is now a first API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 278.92,
          "end": 280.61,
          "en": "as we could write it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 280.61,
          "end": 285.19,
          "en": "An API route for extracting an incoming email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 285.19,
          "end": 288.36,
          "en": "Now we wanna send a request to this API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 288.36,
          "end": 289.65,
          "en": "and we wanna do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 289.65,
          "end": 292.38,
          "en": "from inside the components input folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 292.38,
          "end": 295.54,
          "en": "from inside the newsletter registration file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 295.54,
          "end": 297.99,
          "en": "Here we have the registration handler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 297.99,
          "end": 301.1,
          "en": "which is triggered when the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 301.1,
          "end": 304.06,
          "en": "And here I am preventing the browser default then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 304.06,
          "end": 307.04,
          "en": "to a wide that the page has reloaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 307.04,
          "end": 310.74,
          "en": "Now we could also validate the user input here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 310.74,
          "end": 313.52,
          "en": "and show an error message if it is invalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 313.52,
          "end": 317.85,
          "en": "again, validation here is then just a convenience feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 317.85,
          "end": 320.34,
          "en": "to show some feedback to the user quickly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 320.34,
          "end": 322.77,
          "en": "It's not something you should rely on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 322.77,
          "end": 324.81,
          "en": "and it's not something I will add here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 324.81,
          "end": 327.69,
          "en": "because it has nothing to do with API routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 327.69,
          "end": 330.623,
          "en": "but of course feel free to add it in your solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 331.93,
          "end": 334.54,
          "en": "Now, in my case here, I will not add it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 334.54,
          "end": 338.6,
          "en": "I instead wanna send that HTTP request to the API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 338.6,
          "end": 340.01,
          "en": "we just added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 340.01,
          "end": 341.61,
          "en": "And again we can, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 341.61,
          "end": 343.33,
          "en": "do this with the fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 343.33,
          "end": 345.023,
          "en": "which is built into the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 345.9,
          "end": 349.92,
          "en": "Now for the URL you'll learned that the API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 349.92,
          "end": 353.85,
          "en": "is hosted by the same server as our pages are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 353.85,
          "end": 356.55,
          "en": "sent back from so it's the same domain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 356.55,
          "end": 359.37,
          "en": "And hence can just construct an absolute path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 359.37,
          "end": 364.37,
          "en": "to the API route with /api/newsletter in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 365.5,
          "end": 370.5,
          "en": "/newsletter because I named my API route file, newsletter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 371.25,
          "end": 373.5,
          "en": "If you named it differently you have to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 373.5,
          "end": 376.923,
          "en": "a different identifier here in your URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 378.49,
          "end": 380.76,
          "en": "Now we wanna send a post request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 380.76,
          "end": 384.2,
          "en": "because we need to add some data to the outgoing requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 384.2,
          "end": 389.2,
          "en": "and hence here all at this configuration object to fetch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 389.3,
          "end": 393.46,
          "en": "where we can set methods to post and then add a body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 393.46,
          "end": 397.45,
          "en": "Now, speaking of that body, we need to get access to the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 397.45,
          "end": 399.15,
          "en": "input value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 399.15,
          "end": 401.71,
          "en": "And there are two main ways of doing that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 401.71,
          "end": 406.14,
          "en": "we can add state and update the state with every keystroke",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 406.14,
          "end": 408.73,
          "en": "or we use a ref and I'll do the letter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 408.73,
          "end": 411.22,
          "en": "since I only need access to the input once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 411.22,
          "end": 412.763,
          "en": "when the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 413.76,
          "end": 415.6,
          "en": "So for this I'll use useRef,",
          "zh": ""
        },
